|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Sweep other projects on padme and doudou for review-pr, review-pr-prose and gaze-as-gate wording; one PR per affected project, repointing to gaze plus verify-gate. Authorized writes, this purpose only. No stub skill. | 1.5 | 0.5 |
| 1 | Evidence core: forge actor contract (allow-list of three pinned actor IDs, fail closed), shared reuse script, verify-gate stale and no-report checks, seat table, risk floor, report hashes in the block, behavioural regression tests. | 3.5 | 0.5 |
| 2 | Gaze rebuilt as the review entry: inline, transport preflight with detached fallback, controller-written artifacts, validated return schema; review-pr's code panel becomes the code mode; old battery and `agents/gaze-pr-review.md` deleted; portable simplify a declared seat. | 3.5 | 0.4 |
| 3 | Retire review-pr in one merge wave (move, IDH_ROOT fix, hunt, references, lint), installed-link cleanup, read-only audit of installed registrations. Waits for child 0's PRs. | 3.5 | 0.5 |
| — | One measured raid with the new timings. | | 0.25 |
| 4 | Conditional prose fold: only if the measured raid or a drift test shows the panel bodies diverging; retire review-pr-prose, extend the lint. | (2.5) | (0.4) |

Committed: about 12 agent-hours and 2.15 author-hours. Ticket 1099
(bounded review time) follows and is blocked by this ticket.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Hunt produces and executes the justified review plan, with explicit
      reuse/invalidation decisions tied to revisions and affected scope.
- [ ] Gaze is the single review skill; review-pr is retired with no alias and
      the retired-name lint fails on any live reference.
- [ ] verify-gate still blocks missing criteria, unresolved blocking findings
      (Copilot's included) and absent required proof; merge remains a
      separate caller decision; a test shows gaze never returns APPROVED.
- [ ] Regression scenarios demonstrate unchanged-head reuse without duplicate
      reviewers, proportionate re-review after relevant changes, and rejection
      of stale/missing proof. They test behavior, not wording alone.
- [ ] Child 0's project PRs merged before review-pr is retired.
- [ ] Affected skills, profiles, callers, documentation and catalog updated;
      integration of the children verified before this tracker closes.

## Tentative proposal — review storage and delivery (2026-10-15)

Author-requested discussion note only, subject to compatibility with
`docs/discussions/2026-10-14-1096-design.md`, which was not read during
this discussion. This does not supersede the adopted specification.

- Store tracked reports under
  `reviews/<base-short>..<head-short>/<agent>-<angle>.md`: one directory
  per reviewed range, one report per agent and angle.
- Use SHA abbreviations of at least six characters, extended when needed
  for uniqueness; preserve the complete base/head SHAs in each report.
- Reviewers work in their own worktrees and return their final reports via
  CLI stdout or structured final-result output. The launcher captures and
  validates the result and writes the file in the orchestrator's worktree,
  without requiring reviewers to write into that worktree.
- Commit the collected reports on the delivery branch so they travel with
  the code/PR. Report commits follow the reviewed head and are outside the
  reviewed range.

Reconcile this option with the specification's transport, controller-written
artifact, evidence and reuse contracts before adoption. Existing exit
criteria remain unchanged.

## Author decision — repository-backed review reports (2026-10-15)

Following the specification read and discussion, the author adopts the
`reviews/<base-short>..<head-short>/<agent>-<angle>.md` layout and
launcher-collected final reports described above. The preceding tentative
status is superseded by this decision.

- Trust in reviewers is presumed by default; this change introduces no
  additional reviewer-authentication or signing requirement.
- Preserve the full reviewed base/head SHAs. Adding report files in a later
  commit does not by itself invalidate the review: validation must establish
  that subsequent changes are confined to review artifacts. Changes to
  reviewed content or relevant context remain subject to the existing
  invalidation/reuse contract. Final checks and the gate remain tied to the
  delivered revision.
- This explicitly revises the design's choice of forge comments instead of
  branch files as the report store. Reconcile the specification and evidence
  implementation accordingly; a changed HEAD alone is not sufficient to
  reject otherwise valid review evidence.
- CLI reports are captured by the launcher; external GitHub Copilot reviews
  require API ingestion preserving source links, IDs and reviewed revision.
  Copilot remains binding external feedback, not a planned panel seat or an
  independence contribution.

This records an authorized design choice, not an implemented feature.
Container/CI delivery, cross-host transport and Copilot ingestion still
require implementation review. The implementation ticket stays open.
